  "instance_name": "school_drop_off",
  "label": "School Drop-Off as a Common Parenting Ritual",
  "description": "The phrase 'your mom dropped you off to school' references a universal, everyday parenting activity. This is a cultural norm in many societies, particularly in Western countries, where parents drop off their children at school in the morning. The meme uses this common scenario to set up the punchline, making the absurdity of the fine more relatable and therefore funnier. This cultural context is not visible in the image but is essential to understanding the joke.",
